{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264958,"nonce":"9pQNS2CmqTdGLJYQhwZbSg8zOTM=","title":"GPU plugin: wgpu's unsafe-only entry points","message":"wgpu 30 makes a few things `unsafe`, and the plugin does not expose them\nbecause it cannot check their conditions for the caller:\n\n- `LoadOp::DontCare`: needs a token; undefined contents are read if the\n  program relies on them.\n- Pipeline caches: `Device::create_pipeline_cache` trusts data from a\n  previous `PipelineCache::get_data` on the same adapter and driver.\n- Passthrough shaders (`PASSTHROUGH_SHADERS`): raw SPIR-V, MSL, DXIL or HLSL\n  that naga does not validate.\n- Backend handle interop (`as_hal`, `create_*_from_hal`).\n\nExperimental features are different: wgpu's condition is only the program's\nacceptance, and requesting an `EXPERIMENTAL_*` native feature is that\nacceptance (7626bee). The entries above need a decision on whether and how a\nprogram opts in, per device or per call, without adding defines or\nenvironment variables.","files":null}]}